{
  "case_id": "2019-18-1195",
  "document_hash": "0597122142351827cafb88f5e6cdb23963dbc0ee4e09eb4e99b086f1525a9b40",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1195",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0597122142351827cafb88f5e6cdb23963dbc0ee4e09eb4e99b086f1525a9b40",
      "evidence_id": "ev-059712214235-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:05 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Richard D. Komer",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1195",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0597122142351827cafb88f5e6cdb23963dbc0ee4e09eb4e99b086f1525a9b40",
      "evidence_id": "ev-059712214235-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This case asks whether the Federal Constitution allows the wholesale exclusion of religious schools from scholarship programs. It does not."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1195",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0597122142351827cafb88f5e6cdb23963dbc0ee4e09eb4e99b086f1525a9b40",
      "evidence_id": "ev-059712214235-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "May -- may I ask you some threshold questions about Article III standing? Under the Montana judgment, these parents are treated no differently than parents of children who are going to secular private schools, so where is the harm?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Jeffrey B. Wall",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1195",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0597122142351827cafb88f5e6cdb23963dbc0ee4e09eb4e99b086f1525a9b40",
      "evidence_id": "ev-059712214235-0000-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Montana Supreme Court held that the Montana constitution requires religious discrimination that the federal constitution forbids."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Jeffrey B. Wall",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1195",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0597122142351827cafb88f5e6cdb23963dbc0ee4e09eb4e99b086f1525a9b40",
      "evidence_id": "ev-059712214235-0000-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If the Montana Supreme Court had invalidated this program because it included historically African-American schools or all-girl schools, that would be a straightforward equal-protection violation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1195",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0597122142351827cafb88f5e6cdb23963dbc0ee4e09eb4e99b086f1525a9b40",
      "evidence_id": "ev-059712214235-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Perhaps you could comment, counsel."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1195",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0597122142351827cafb88f5e6cdb23963dbc0ee4e09eb4e99b086f1525a9b40",
      "evidence_id": "ev-059712214235-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: My hypothetical was they give it out in -- it's called the Public School System of the United States. I'm saying that's what I'm talking about. Now, what's your response? What's the difference between this case, you win, and the same with the public schools, they have to give it to parochial schools too. What's the difference?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent (Adam G. Unikowski)",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1195",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0597122142351827cafb88f5e6cdb23963dbc0ee4e09eb4e99b086f1525a9b40",
      "evidence_id": "ev-059712214235-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Constitution does not bar the State of Montana from enacting and applying a state constitutional provision that keeps its own state legislature out of the business of funding of religious schools."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent (Adam G. Unikowski)",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1195",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0597122142351827cafb88f5e6cdb23963dbc0ee4e09eb4e99b086f1525a9b40",
      "evidence_id": "ev-059712214235-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The first reason is that the coercion aspect of Trinity Lutheran, which was crucial to the Court's decision, was absent here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1195",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0597122142351827cafb88f5e6cdb23963dbc0ee4e09eb4e99b086f1525a9b40",
      "evidence_id": "ev-059712214235-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: And why is it different from other hypothetical?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1195",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0597122142351827cafb88f5e6cdb23963dbc0ee4e09eb4e99b086f1525a9b40",
      "evidence_id": "ev-059712214235-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: How is that -- how is that consistent with the principle set forth in Trinity Lutheran or McDaniel, Justice Brennan's concurrence in McDaniel?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1195",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0597122142351827cafb88f5e6cdb23963dbc0ee4e09eb4e99b086f1525a9b40",
      "evidence_id": "ev-059712214235-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Where has it said -- where has it said that that's not how it's construed?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1195",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0597122142351827cafb88f5e6cdb23963dbc0ee4e09eb4e99b086f1525a9b40",
      "evidence_id": "ev-059712214235-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: May I ask you a question? Let's go back to the basic, okay?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1195",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0597122142351827cafb88f5e6cdb23963dbc0ee4e09eb4e99b086f1525a9b40",
      "evidence_id": "ev-059712214235-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: No, isn't the crucial question why the state court did what it did?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1195",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0597122142351827cafb88f5e6cdb23963dbc0ee4e09eb4e99b086f1525a9b40",
      "evidence_id": "ev-059712214235-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "One is to Justice Breyer's question, just funding religion, funding religious schools generally or training of clergy is -- is an establishment clause concern, but this -- it's a separate issue when you set up a neutral benefit program -- police, fire, or scholarships -- and allow people to use those things, allow religious institutions to obtain the benefits of those things on a non-discriminatory basis."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1195",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0597122142351827cafb88f5e6cdb23963dbc0ee4e09eb4e99b086f1525a9b40",
      "evidence_id": "ev-059712214235-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: You think that was the design of the no-aid clause, to -- to help religious institutions?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1195",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0597122142351827cafb88f5e6cdb23963dbc0ee4e09eb4e99b086f1525a9b40",
      "evidence_id": "ev-059712214235-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Well, no one's compelling the religious schools to participate in a program in order to accept funds from the program, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1195",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0597122142351827cafb88f5e6cdb23963dbc0ee4e09eb4e99b086f1525a9b40",
      "evidence_id": "ev-059712214235-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: So a religious school that doesn't want to be part of a neutral program doesn't have to be."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1195",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0597122142351827cafb88f5e6cdb23963dbc0ee4e09eb4e99b086f1525a9b40",
      "evidence_id": "ev-059712214235-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: I think the other side's argument is the way you can do better is to say: If we're going to give benefits to private schools, which you don't have to do -- to Justice Breyer's question, you do not have to"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1195",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0597122142351827cafb88f5e6cdb23963dbc0ee4e09eb4e99b086f1525a9b40",
      "evidence_id": "ev-059712214235-0003-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Mr. Unikowsky, if we can just go back to the standing question."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Amicus",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1195",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "document_hash": "0597122142351827cafb88f5e6cdb23963dbc0ee4e09eb4e99b086f1525a9b40",
      "evidence_id": "ev-059712214235-0003-0014",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "But, of course, this argument is made in amicus brief."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1195",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0597122142351827cafb88f5e6cdb23963dbc0ee4e09eb4e99b086f1525a9b40",
      "evidence_id": "ev-059712214235-0003-0012",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They focus on the religious affiliation or religious nature of the schools. They are not talking about what the schools do. They are talking about what the schools are."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1195",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0597122142351827cafb88f5e6cdb23963dbc0ee4e09eb4e99b086f1525a9b40",
      "evidence_id": "ev-059712214235-0003-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 71
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: It's almost sort of a illusory state, isn't it? The legislatures can choose to give money or not. If they choose, they have to do it this way."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1195",
      "confidence": 0.0,
